# Terms over the centers of groups (D139): [[energy.bond]],
# [[energy.angle]], and [[energy.dihedral]] with `groups`, masks of Amber,
# in place of `particles`, whose centers, weighted by mass or alike, are the
# members of one tuple; a bond takes the components dx, dy, dz of the vector
# from the first center to the second besides r. Each center is the
# weighted mean of its particles in the minimum image from the one in the
# middle of them by number, and the centers are taken from the first, so
# that a group that lies across a face of the cell has its center. The
# energy is a function of sums over pairs of particles, and its forces and
# virial follow from the derivatives of the energy with respect to the sums
# (D2). On the dipeptide: a bond between the centers of mass of the peptide
# and of a water, in r and dz; an angle between the centers of geometry of
# its three residues; and a dihedral with the fifth residue. Then the same
# with the coordinates moved by half the box and folded into it, which puts
# the peptide across three faces: the same energies. check_centroid.py
# computes the energies, the forces on every particle of a group against
# central differences, and the virial, from the forces of each term and the
# images that it takes. The file of `pull_coordinates` (D145) of a run
# with energies: its first line against the coordinates, the energies,
# and central differences of each term.
#
# REQUIRES: hdf5
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/dipeptide/dipeptide.prmtop %S/Inputs/dipeptide/dipeptide.inpcrd %t
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %s | sed '1d;$d' > %t/terms.toml
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- terms/p' %s | sed '1d;$d' | sed 's/terms.h5/plain.h5/' > %t/plain.toml
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run plain.toml > plain.log && mdir run terms.toml > terms.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/terms.log
# RUN: mdir checkpoint --print=forces %t/plain.h5 > %t/plain.forces
# RUN: mdir checkpoint --print=forces %t/terms.h5 > %t/terms.forces
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_centroid.py %t/dipeptide.prmtop %t/dipeptide.inpcrd %t/plain.forces %t/terms.forces %t/plain.log %t/terms.log | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PYTHON
#
# RUN: sed -e 's/^energy_interval = 0/energy_interval = 1\npull_coordinates = "pull.dat"/' -e 's/terms.h5/pull.h5/' %t/terms.toml > %t/pull.toml
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run pull.toml > pull.log
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_centroid.py --pull %t/dipeptide.prmtop %t/dipeptide.inpcrd %t/pull.dat | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PULL
#
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/shift_inpcrd.py %t/dipeptide.inpcrd > %t/shifted.inpcrd
# RUN: sed -e 's/dipeptide.inpcrd/shifted.inpcrd/' -e 's/terms.h5/shifted.h5/' %t/terms.toml > %t/shifted.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's/dipeptide.inpcrd/shifted.inpcrd/' -e 's/plain.h5/shifted-plain.h5/' %t/plain.toml > %t/shifted-plain.toml
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run shifted-plain.toml > shifted-plain.log && mdir run shifted.toml > shifted.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/shifted.log
# RUN: mdir checkpoint --print=forces %t/shifted-plain.h5 > %t/shifted-plain.forces
# RUN: mdir checkpoint --print=forces %t/shifted.h5 > %t/shifted.forces
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_centroid.py %t/dipeptide.prmtop %t/shifted.inpcrd %t/shifted-plain.forces %t/shifted.forces %t/shifted-plain.log %t/shifted.log | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PYTHON
